Let $(M,g)$ be a two-dimensional Riemannian manifold, possibly with boundary, and let $G_M(x,y)$ denote a hydrodynamic Green's function of the Laplace–Beltrami operator on $M$ (chosen so as to incorporate the appropriate boundary conditions when $\partial M \neq \emptyset$, and a neutralizing background when $M$ is closed). A system of $N$ point vortices on $M$ with strengths $\Gamma_1,\dots,\Gamma_N \in \mathbb{R}\setminus\{0\}$ at positions $x_1(t),\dots,x_N(t) \in M$ evolves according to the Hamiltonian system
$$\Gamma_i\, \omega(\dot x_i, \cdot) = d_{x_i} H(x_1,\dots,x_N), \qquad H = \sum_{i<j} \Gamma_i \Gamma_j\, G_M(x_i,x_j) + \tfrac{1}{2}\sum_i \Gamma_i^2 R(x_i),$$
where $\omega$ is the Riemannian area form and $R(x) = \lim_{y\to x}\bigl(G_M(x,y) + \tfrac{1}{2\pi}\log d(x,y)\bigr)$ is the Robin function.

Carry out a systematic study, for small numbers $N$ (say $N \in \{2,3,4,5\}$) of point vortices, of the resulting dynamics, relative equilibria, and their bifurcations (as positions, strengths, or geometric parameters of $M$ are varied) on each of the following domains:
(i) the half-plane $\{(x,y)\in\mathbb{R}^2 : y>0\}$;
(ii) the quarter-plane $\{(x,y)\in\mathbb{R}^2 : x>0,\ y>0\}$;
(iii) the hemisphere $\{x\in S^2 : x_3 \geq 0\}$;
(iv) the quarter-sphere $\{x\in S^2 : x_2,x_3 \geq 0\}$;
(v) the round disk $\{(x,y)\in\mathbb{R}^2 : x^2+y^2<1\}$;
(vi) the flat torus $\mathbb{R}^2/(a\mathbb{Z}\oplus b\mathbb{Z})$ for varying aspect ratio $a/b$;
(vii) the infinite cylinder $\mathbb{R}\times(\mathbb{R}/\mathbb{Z})$;
(viii) the half-cylinder $[0,\infty)\times(\mathbb{R}/\mathbb{Z})$.

For each geometry, classify equilibria and relative equilibria, determine their linear and nonlinear stability, and describe the bifurcation diagrams as the strengths $\Gamma_i$ and the geometric parameters are varied.

